export const meta = {
  name: 'ajcr-phase4-design',
  description: 'Design the remaining Phase-4 producers: divisor descent, canonical evaluator, family openness',
  phases: [{ title: 'Design' }],
}

const ROOT = '/home/axel/LeanAlgebraicGeometry-Horizon/MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild'

const COMMON = `You are designing the next Lean 4 formalization step in ${ROOT} (package AlgebraicJacobian, mathlib v4.31, lake project at that root). Relative Picard functor of a smooth proper geometrically irreducible curve C over a field k; the rank-one Abel route. You are READ-ONLY: do not edit any file. You may use grep/read tools and the horizon search CLI ("$HORIZON_BIN" search "<words>" --json) to find existing lemmas (HORIZON_BIN env var is set).
Current state facts (verified): PicRankOneOpen pi : Subfunctor (picDegLayerFunctor C (genus C)) with membership = every affine pullback carries a PicRankOneLocalPresentation (file Picard/Pic0RankOneLocus.lean). PicRankOneLocalPresentation (Picard/Pic0RankOnePresentation.lean) has cover : Algebra.EtaleCover A, datum : BasicOpenCocycleDatum C cover.Carrier pi, h1_vanishing/h0_finite/h0_projective/h0_rank_one over cover.Carrier, native_pushforward_base_change over every cartesian square. Landed: exists_glued_rankOne_away_divisor_with_abel_evaluation (Picard/Pic0RankOneFibrePresentedProducerFiniteGlue.lean) produces F0 : DivFamZarAff C P.cover.Carrier (genus C) with abelDivAffPlus C P.cover.Carrier F0 = PicEtAff.mapAlg C (Algebra.ofId A cover.Carrier) (picEtAffineEquiv C A lam.1), plus relPicMk F0.picClass = P.representative, under [IsNoetherianRing P.cover.Carrier]. The big-site consumer scaffold (Picard/Pic0RankOneFibrePresentedProducer.lean): PicRankOneEvaluationDivisorData pi = {divisor : rankOneLocus ⟶ rankOneDivisorLocus, divisor_abel : divisor ≫ rankOneAbelSigma pi = 𝟙}; then per-(X,g) PicRankOneFibrePresentationInput + EvaluationDivisorPullback (IsPullback squares) feed picRankOneOpen_isOpen_of_evaluationDivisorPullbackFamilies : PicRankOneOpen.IsOpen pi.
Deliverable: a concrete implementation plan an implementer can follow WITHOUT re-deriving your research: exact new declaration signatures (Lean syntax), exact existing lemmas to invoke (fully-qualified, with file), the proof skeleton per declaration (5-15 lines of math+tactic outline each), the hard steps flagged with fallback options, and a dependency order. Cite ONLY declarations you have verified exist by reading/grepping/searching — never invent a lemma name. Your final text goes to an orchestrator.`

phase('Design')
const briefs = [
  {key: 'descend-divisor', model: 'fable', prompt: `${COMMON}
DESIGN TASK A — descend the glued rank-one divisor from the etale cover carrier to the base ring A, and prove presentation independence.
The glued F0 lives over P.cover.Carrier (a faithfully flat etale A-algebra). Needed (shape, adjust as you see fit): theorem exists_rankOne_divisor_over_base (P : PicRankOneLocalPresentation pi lam) [suitable Noetherian hyps] : exists F : DivFamZarAff C A (genus C), abelDivAffPlus C A F = picEtAffineEquiv C A lam.1 (and a picClass tie), plus generator/presentation independence: two presentations P P' of the same lam give the same F.
Investigate: (1) What descent/uniqueness infrastructure exists for DivFamZarAff along faithfully flat or etale maps — grep for descent, faithfullyFlat, EtaleCover in Picard/ and Cohomology/; read DivRepClassifyZarAffSep.lean, DivRepClassifyZarSep.lean, DivRepAffPull*.lean, DivisorFamilyAff*.lean for injectivity/descent of families; look for lemmas like mapAlg injectivity, DivFamZarAff.mapAlg_injective, eq_of_faithfullyFlat, or a sheaf property of divFunctorAff for the etale topology. (2) KEY mathematical lever: in a rank-one class (h0 = 1 after every field base change), the effective divisor with a given Abel image is UNIQUE — is there a uniqueness theorem for divisors with equal abelDivAffPlus image / equal picClass + fibrewise degree? grep for uniqueness in DivisorFamilyDegreeZeroUnique.lean, ComparisonUnique.lean, DivRepChartClassUniv*.lean. (3) Whether uniqueness + fppf/Zariski-local existence gives descent WITHOUT full etale descent machinery: e.g. does DivFamZarAff satisfy a separated-presheaf property (mapAlg injective for faithfully flat A → B)? If F0 descends uniquely on a cover where two pullbacks agree by uniqueness, plan the exact gluing statement. Also determine where [IsNoetherianRing cover.Carrier] can come from for an arbitrary CommRing A test (it cannot in general!) — check how existing consumers handle this (maybe A restricted to finite type? or fg-subalgebra reduction like RankOneFamilyCertificatesActualDatum does — read that reduction pattern and assess whether the divisor construction can be pushed through the same fg-descent).`},
  {key: 'evaluator-nat', model: 'fable', prompt: `${COMMON}
DESIGN TASK B — produce the canonical evaluator E : PicRankOneEvaluationDivisorData pi (the global natural transformation divisor : rankOneLocus ⟶ rankOneDivisorLocus with divisor ≫ rankOneAbelSigma = id), assuming Task A delivers, for every affine test (A, lam ∈ PicRankOneOpen), a unique F_A(lam) : DivFamZarAff C A (genus C) with abelDivAffPlus C A (F_A lam) = lam's class and uniqueness (any F' with the same Abel image equals F_A lam).
Read Pic0RankOneFibrePresentedProducer.lean FULLY first: exact definitions of rankOneAmbient, rankOneLocus, rankOneDivisorLocus, rankOneAbelSigma, rankOneDivisorToAmbient, PicRankOneEvaluationDivisorData, AbelInverse, evaluationIso. Determine: (1) what a point of rankOneLocus over an arbitrary scheme X actually is (Over.sigmaExtension unfolding — read Over/SigmaExtension source in this project or mathlib as needed); (2) what a point of rankOneDivisorLocus is (presumably a point of the divisor-side subfunctor over yoneda of divRepAffGenusScheme — is it universal-property-based, i.e. a map X ⟶ divRepAffGenusScheme.left landing in the preimage subfunctor?); (3) how to define divisor.app on non-affine X: does the affine-local uniqueness give Zariski gluing on X via the representer (a map to the representing scheme glues iff it glues Zariski-locally — yoneda is a Zariski sheaf; find the exact gluing lemma used elsewhere, e.g. in DivisorFamilyAffMap.lean map_comp via exists_isPullbackValue/pullbackValue_unique, or Scheme.LocalRepresentability / openCoverHomGlue-type lemmas — grep Scheme.homOfOpenCover, Scheme.OpenCover.glueMorphisms); (4) the naturality proof obligations and the divisor_abel section law; (5) then the AbelInverse law (divisor after abel = id on rankOneDivisorLocus) — this is uniqueness of effective divisor in its class again. Produce the full declaration list with signatures and proof skeletons, dependency-ordered.`},
  {key: 'family-openness', model: 'fable', prompt: `${COMMON}
DESIGN TASK C — the family-openness input: for every scheme X and g : yoneda.obj X ⟶ rankOneAmbient (the Σ-extension of picDegLayerFunctor C (genus C)), produce the open W : X.Opens on which the class is rank-one presented, i.e. inhabit PicRankOneFibrePresentationInput pi E g and prove EvaluationDivisorPullback (the IsPullback square), feeding picRankOneOpen_isOpen_of_evaluationDivisorPullbackFamilies.
This is the semicontinuity step: W = locus where h0 of the fibre is 1 and H1 vanishes (equivalently, by degree-genus Riemann-Roch, the locus where the fibrewise h0 is minimal). Investigate what exists: (1) grep/search for semicontinuity, upperSemicontinuous, rankAtStalk locus openness, Module.rankAtStalk open, FiniteProjective locus, in the whole tree and in mathlib (Mathlib.RingTheory.LocalProperties, Mathlib.Topology.LocallyConstant, Module.rankAtStalk — e.g. mathlib lemmas that rankAtStalk of a finite projective module is locally constant); (2) how h1_vanishing propagates: is there a cohomology-and-base-change/openness result in Cohomology/ (grep H1Vanishing locus, exists_fg_pairH1_vanishing_stage, GluedSheafH0BaseChange) letting the H1=0 + h0-rank-1 condition spread from a point to a basic open of the test; (3) the already-landed openness pattern: read Pic0RankOneLocus*.lean siblings and DivRankOneOpen*.lean and any DivRankOneOpen producer attempts, plus files whose names mention Open/Locus (Pic0ChartLocusH0Rank.lean, DivSchemeQProj.lean) for how earlier lanes proved openness of similar loci — extract reusable lemmas; (4) whether the route can avoid full semicontinuity by using the translated-cover structure (the locus is a union of translates of one open; openness of ONE canonical open on the representer might suffice — check what pic0RepresentableByOfCharts in Pic0SigmaSheaf.lean actually needs). Flag honestly what has NO existing substrate and estimate which missing pieces are mathlib-shaped vs project-shaped. Produce the plan.`},
  {key: 'rooting-audit', model: 'opus', prompt: `${COMMON}
DESIGN TASK D — rooting and audit plan for Pic0CriticalPath.lean. Read ${ROOT}/AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/Pic0CriticalPath.lean fully (imports, #check list, #print axioms list, docstring). Then determine which landed critical-route modules/endpoints are NOT yet imported/checked there. Candidates to verify exist and inspect: Pic0RankOneNativePresentationSplit.lean (mem_picRankOneOpen_of_isSplitWitness), Pic0RankOneNativeBaseChangeCartesian.lean (isIso_canonicalBaseChangeMap_nativeModule, PicRankOneNativePresentation.ofCertificatesWithNativeBaseChange), Pic0RankOneFamilyCertificatesActualDatum.lean, Cohomology/RankOneFamilyCertificatesActualDatum.lean (RankOneFamilyCertificates.ofActualDatum), Cohomology/RankOneFamilyCertificatesActualDatumRank.lean, Pic0RankOneFibrePresentedProducerAwayNaturality.lean (baseOpenRankOneDivisor_awayMul_compat, baseOpenRankOneDivisor_mapAlgHom_mul_left), Pic0RankOneFibrePresentedProducerFiniteGlue.lean (exists_glued_rankOne_away_divisor_with_abel_evaluation), Pic0RankOneFibrePresentedProducerSectionDivEq.lean, Pic0RankOneFibrePresentedProducer.lean (PicRankOneEvaluationDivisorData, picRankOneOpen_isOpen_of_evaluationDivisorPullbackFamilies), Pic0RankOneNativePresentationOfLocal.lean, Pic0RankOneNativePresentationField.lean, Pic0RankOneNativePresentationDatum.lean, and the new Pic0RankOneTranslatedCoverMembership.lean (exists_sepClosedTranslated_mem_picRankOneOpen — just added, not yet built). Also check the docstring claims that are now stale (it says the canonical divisor/Abel iso/sepclosed cover endpoints do not exist — the membership endpoint now exists). Output: (1) the exact import lines to add; (2) the exact #check lines to add (fully qualified names, verified by grep); (3) the exact #print axioms lines to add for NEW endpoint theorems (not every helper — the endpoints per the reviewer contract); (4) a rewritten docstring paragraph reflecting the new state honestly (no overclaim: openness/rankOneAbelIso/representability still missing); (5) any #check in the current root that would now FAIL (renamed/deleted decls). Do not edit files.`},
]

const results = await parallel(briefs.map(b => () =>
  agent(b.prompt, {label: `design:${b.key}`, phase: 'Design', model: b.model})
))
return Object.fromEntries(briefs.map((b, i) => [b.key, results[i]]))

